pageType: content
background: { type: solid, color: "$paper" }
notes: |
  Slide 3: Nearly a Decade of Observing: Run Timeline O1 to O4b.
  - Reviews the four observing eras: O1 (2015-2016), O2 (2016-2017), O3 (2019-2020), and O4 (2023-2025).
  - Details the instrumental upgrades at each commissioning gate: laser power increases (20W to 70W), monolithic silica suspension fiber upgrades, frequency-independent squeezing (2-3 dB), and 300 m filter cavities for frequency-dependent squeezing.
  - Highlights sensitivity evolution: Binary Neutron Star (BNS) range expanded from 70 Mpc in O1 to 160 Mpc in O4.
  - Explains the cubic volume scaling law: search volume scales as range cubed, yielding a ~12-fold increase in accessible cosmic volume.
