  - elementId: gates-box
    elementType: shape
    shapeName: rect
    bounds: [185, 170, 420, 160]
    fill: { type: solid, color: "$highlightBg" }
    border: { style: solid, width: 1, color: "$border" }

  - elementId: gates-txt
    elementType: text
    bounds: [195, 178, 400, 145]
    content:
      fontSize: 9
      lineHeight: 1.35
      color: "$ink"
      text: |
        <b>Key Commissioning Upgrades Across Gates:</b><br/>
        • <b>Gate 1 (O1 → O2)</b>: Laser power increased from 20 W to 40 W; monolithic fused-silica suspensions replaced steel wires, attenuating thermal suspension noise.<br/>
        • <b>Gate 2 (O2 → O3)</b>: Introduction of frequency-independent squeezed vacuum states (2–3 dB), directly lowering high-frequency photon shot noise.<br/>
        • <b>Gate 3 (O3 → O4)</b>: 300 m optical filter cavities deployed at Hanford and Livingston for frequency-dependent squeezing (4.6–6.1 dB); laser power increased to 70 W; high-reflectivity mirror coatings to lower Brownian noise.

  # Volume Scaling Box
  - elementId: vol-box
    elementType: shape
    shapeName: rect
    bounds: [185, 345, 420, 90]
    fill: { type: solid, color: "$cardBg" }
    border: { style: solid, width: 1, color: "$primary" }

  - elementId: vol-txt
    elementType: text
    bounds: [195, 350, 400, 85]
    content:
      fontSize: 9.5
      lineHeight: 1.3
      color: "$ink"
      text: |
        <b>Cosmic Volume Scaling Law:</b><br/>
        Detection volume scales as the cube of the BNS horizon:
        <p>\( V_{\text{search}} \propto R_{\text{BNS}}^3 \Rightarrow (160/70)^3 \approx 11.9 \times \text{ cosmic volume increase} \)</p>
        Every 20% gain in strain sensitivity nearly doubles the observed event rate.

